From 3b261fa7dde1b707f817b96fe54d5fc81b4c70d3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: caoanhhao <dev@skyperry.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 22:11:39 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 315/315] drm/msm/a6xx: raise the a650 hang detection threshold

Where Winds Meet lost its Vulkan device after ~15 min of play: the RBBM
interface hang interrupt fired with only the shader pipeline busy (SP,
HLSQ, VFD, VPC, PC, RB; no UCHE, TP or VBIF traffic) and msm killed the
submit. kgsl raised the a650 threshold from 0x3fffff to 0xcfffff because
older a6xx falsely report a hang on long running payloads; upstream msm
still uses 0x1fffff for it. Use 0xcfffff, as for a612 and a7xx. A real
hang is still caught, by the same interrupt or by the hangcheck timer.

caoanhhao used AI to code
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gpu.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gpu.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gpu.c
index 6d1778f82..353847484 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gpu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gpu.c
@@ -1360,8 +1360,12 @@ static int hw_init(struct msm_gpu *gpu)
 
 	a6xx_set_ubwc_config(gpu);
 
-	/* Enable fault detection */
+	/*
+	 * Enable fault detection. a650 falsely reports an interface hang on long
+	 * running work with the shorter threshold (kgsl uses 0xcfffff there too).
+	 */
 	if (adreno_is_a612(adreno_gpu) ||
+	    adreno_is_a650(adreno_gpu) ||
 	    adreno_is_a722(adreno_gpu) ||
 	    adreno_is_a730(adreno_gpu) ||
 	    adreno_is_a740_family(adreno_gpu))
